include "../../linux.mereo"

-- REFUSED: `likely` predicts a CONDITION, and a named scope has none.
--
-- `likely` means here what it means in C: a hint about which way a branch is
-- expected to go. It rides on the guard of a conditional scope -- `n == 5
-- likely goes` -- and there is nothing for it to say about a scope that is
-- entered unconditionally.
--
-- This was `LABEL likely goes`, which used to open a crossroad. That machinery
-- is gone: an if/else is a conditional scope that leaves early, and what
-- follows it is the other path.
program (arguments) goes
  n is arguments.count
  buf is 8 bytes
  pick likely goes
    n is n + 1
  end
  [buf + 0 : 1] is 48 + n
end
